From 6d7b0a363305a85748290f1a29c0531840845fb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 13:29:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] qos: remove L4S marking and the Wi-Fi downstream (WMM) stamp

L4S was never accepted by the traffic manager on the validated port ("dualq
isn't supported", egress_tm index 6) and its rejection abandoned the whole
class-queue priority correction, leaving the stock inverted layout for as long
as the toggle stayed on. The WMM lift was measured to halve wireless throughput
in both directions (top class on AC_VO defeats aggregation). Both are gone from
the page, the engine, the defaults, the JSON and all 25 dictionaries
(lockstep 6994 -> 6990). The download policer stays, opt-in, and its help now
says a policer drops rather than delays and should stay off on a network that
carries calls. rq_rebuild takes one argument again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
